        <h2>What is a TPI Golf Assessment?</h2>
        <p>TPI stands for the <strong>Titleist Performance Institute</strong> — an organization that studies how the body moves during a golf swing. A TPI assessment is a 13–16 point physical screen (mobility, stability, balance) performed by a TPI-certified physiotherapist or chiropractor, not a golf pro. The results explain which physical limitations — tight hips, restricted thoracic rotation, weak glutes — show up as swing faults or pain, and turn into a treatment plan.</p>
        <p>Because it's delivered by a regulated physio or chiro, it's billed like any other physio/chiro visit — which is why it's worth checking your extended health benefits before assuming it's an out-of-pocket golf lesson.</p>
        <div class="tpi-levels">
          <span class="tpi-badge">TPI Level 1 — general screen</span>
          <span class="tpi-badge">TPI Level 2 — sport-specific</span>
          <span class="tpi-badge">TPI Medical / Level 3 — highest clinical cert</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
